+# Retention planning: summary
+
+## What changed
+
+- `vaultsnap/retention.py`: implemented `plan_retention(snapshots, policy, now)`. It only plans and deletes nothing. `Plan` and the signature are unchanged.
+- `tests/test_retention_adr.py` (new): 13 tests for ADR details the existing suite does not cover. `tests/test_retention.py` is unchanged.
+- `SUMMARY.md`: this file.
+
+Nothing else was touched.
+
+## How each part of the policy was applied
+
+| Part | ADR | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Model, inputs, validation (naive datetimes and `now` raise `ValueError`; duplicate ids raise `ValueError`) | 0001 | Its "Inputs" section |
+| Ordering: later `taken_at` is newer, ties broken by greater id | 0001 | Its "Ordering" section |
+| Empty policy (all five rules off or 0) keeps everything | 0001 | Its "Rules" section |
+| Set-aside: protected-tag snapshots, and snapshots with `taken_at` later than `now`. Kept, never count toward N, never bucket representatives. Exactly `now` is not set aside. | 0001 | Its "Set-aside snapshots" section |
+| `keep_last` = N newest remaining snapshots | 0001 | Its "keep_last" section |
+| Daily, monthly, yearly buckets: N newest non-empty buckets, newest snapshot of each kept; the five rules are unioned | 0001 | Its "Buckets" section |
+| Weekly buckets are ISO weeks (ISO year, ISO week), Monday start | 0003 | Supersedes ADR-0001's Sunday-start "Weeks" section |
+| Bucket date: convert `taken_at` to the fixed `tz_offset_minutes` offset, subtract `day_start_hour`, take the date. All keys derive from it. Ordering, `keep_last` and the `now` check use the real instant. | 0004 | Supersedes ADR-0002 (UTC buckets, now retired) |
+| Output: `keep` and `prune` each newest first, every id in exactly one list | 0001 | Its "Output" section |
+
+ADR-0002 is not applied; ADR-0004 replaces it.
+
+Two details I chose myself:
+- If `now` is not a `datetime` at all, the function raises `TypeError`. The ADRs don't say what to do in that case.
+- Within a bucket, "newest" uses the same ordering as above (`taken_at`, then id), so the representative is well defined.
+
+## What I ran and the results
+
+- `python -m unittest` before the change: 7 errors, all `NotImplementedError`. This was the starting state.
+- `python -m unittest -v` after the change (Python 3.14.3): **Ran 20 tests, OK**. That is the 7 existing tests plus the 13 new ones.
+- `git status --short`: only `vaultsnap/retention.py` (modified) and `tests/test_retention_adr.py` (new) changed, plus `SUMMARY.md`.
+
+Note: my first draft had a bug. With no rules set, it pruned everything. I caught it in review and fixed it with the "empty policy keeps everything" early return. None of the existing tests covered that case, but `test_no_rules_keeps_everything` does now.
+
+## Not verified or unsure
+
+- The new tests pass on the implementation. I did not run mutation checks to confirm each one fails on a wrong implementation, though I checked by hand that the weekly, day-boundary and timezone tests would give different answers under Sunday weeks, UTC buckets and no offset.
+- Only Python 3.14.3 was used. I did not check older Python versions. I also did not look for CI configuration in this repo, so I can't confirm the nightly job's Python version.
+- I did not test against real snapshot data or real timestamps with DST. The offset is fixed by design (ADR-0004 has no DST handling).
+
+## Needs attention outside the allowed files (not changed)
+
+- `README.md` still has the old retention draft that the task said to ignore. It contradicts the ADRs (it describes Sunday weeks and UTC buckets) and should be updated before release.
+- `CHANGELOG.md` says config files "not acted on yet" under 0.2.0. Accurate for that release, and the Unreleased section already covers the new behaviour, so no change is needed there.
